From b679bbe561d154ad799a5b3297d805a686f0068a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NeoTech <andreas@roughedge.se>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 13:44:17 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] fix(geometry): bridge a fill hole to a walk vertex before
 a ray hit

The area preview of a 2D Adaptive with Containment Outside on the
biggest fig8 patch had no fill after #2760 made the fig8 mesh finer.
The hole of that region looks onto a steep, short outer edge. The
computed ray hit on that edge rounds to a point 3e-16 inside the
material, so the ear clipper saw it strictly inside the ears beside it
and stopped with "no ear in a non-triangle walk". A smaller region with
the same edge lost a part of its fill with no error.

merge_hole now tries the walk vertices first, nearest first, and keeps
the ray hits as the last resort. The candidate checks do not change.
The fill is display-only.

Fixes #2762

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
